{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-24 14:47:54 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-24 21:47:54 ICT\n\nVerdict: REJECTED\n\n- **PARTIAL, P1 — Sealed references.** r10 requires seal verification when an *effect* resolves a program-supplied reference, but does not require it when **lift** recognizes a reference and strips its seal before lower issues a new one ([seal rule](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1428), [lift/lower rule](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1447)). A module could export a fabricated reference without using it in an effect; the export lift recursively encodes values ([export rule](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1093)). The specification must require lift to authenticate the reference’s seal and resource kind *before* emitting a UCF resource marker, refusing an invalid reference rather than laundering it into a receiver-sealed capability. Add that export test alongside the existing effect-forgery tests ([M4 tests](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1929)).\n- **CLOSED — Citation and M4 file-box alignment.** The nonexistent “UCF 4.1” citation is corrected to 7.6.2, and the file box now lists the 7.5.1, 7.5.3, and 7.6.2 amendments ([correction](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1397), [file box](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-universal-linker/docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1983)).\n\nThe r10 file passes pure-ASCII and 80-column checks. **Consensus has not been reached; it is not ready to commit.**"}}
